{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The deviation is established as 1.40 km, and it is over the tolerance: POL-RD-22 measures deviation as trip_record.actual_distance_km minus trip_record.optimal_distance_km, the platform's recorded distances, and this record carries 17.60 km actual against 16.20 km recommended. That is above the 1.0 km tolerance POL-RD-22 sets, which puts the case in the 'over 1 km' limb of the POL-RD-24 matrix. The trip record is COMPLETE at weight 1.0, and the GPS trace is not used to re-measure the distance (POL-RD-22).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-06012"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-22"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.actual_distance_km - trip_record.optimal_distance_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-21 requires the driver to inform the rider of a deviation by in-app chat before or at the point of deviation, and provides that where the chat log confirms the rider's acknowledgment the deviation is agreed. The chat shows exactly that: the driver wrote at 10:46:33 'Hi, CTE jam until PIE, I go Upper Thomson then Thomson Road ok?' - a brief reason, which the clause says is enough - and the rider answered at 10:47:03 'Ok can, thanks'. DISCLOSURE under POL-GEN-02(1): the chat artifact is IMPAIRED at weight 0.9; the issue code that fired is SCHEMA_VERSION_MISMATCH (severity LOW), a version tag on an export that is not truncated and whose four messages map one-to-one, and it does not touch the acknowledgement recorded.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-06012", "EV-TRIP-06012"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-21"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.9
    },
    {
      "text": "The notice came before the point of deviation, not after it. The trip record's own event log places route_deviation_detected at 10:49:23 at the CTE / Yio Chu Kang Road exit, and the driver's message was sent at 10:46:33 - nearly three minutes earlier - and read by the rider at 10:47:23, before her reply. The driver's message timestamps are independently carried by the COMPLETE trip record's messages_during_trip block (MSG-06012-003 and MSG-06012-004), so this timing does not depend on the impaired chat export.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-06012", "EV-CHAT-06012"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-21"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.messages_during_trip",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The reroute is traffic-justified on this record under POL-RD-23, which requires a TRAFFIC_ADVISORY that intersects the recommended route and overlaps the trip window. The LTA advisory LTA-TI-261003-6413 is typed HEAVY_TRAFFIC, a congestion class the policy's admissible-type map accepts as justifying a reroute, and it names the Central Expressway (CTE) towards City with a validity window of 10:16:11 to 11:26:11 that overlaps the trip (started 10:36:11, ended 11:04:11) and covers the deviation at 10:49:23. The CTE is a leg of the recommended route (Canberra Link, Seletar Expressway, Central Expressway, Balestier Road), and the driver's trace places the vehicle on the CTE from its first CTE fix at 10:45:11 until 10:48:41, so the advisory intersects the recommended route segment the driver was actually on.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-06012-01", "EV-TRIP-06012", "EV-GPS-06012"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-23"],
      "relies_on": "traffic_advisory.overlaps_trip_window",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Exactly one row of the POL-RD-24 matrix applies, and the evidence fills row (a): the reroute was traffic-justified (POL-RD-23), the rider was informed and agreed (POL-RD-21), and the deviation exceeded 1 km (POL-RD-22). Row (a) provides no refund. Under POL-GEN-03, NO_ACTION is party-relative and never means 'restore a charge': the rider filed, the fare of 21.41 SGD is CHARGED on the ledger and refund_issued_sgd is 0.00, so the present state already reflects the correct outcome - the rider's claim is simply not supported.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-06012", "EV-CHAT-06012", "EV-ADVIS-06012-01", "EV-FARE-06012"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-24", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Row (a) is not displaced by the matrix's escalation carve-out for a case that 'fits no row (for example, informed but the rider objected)'. There was no objection: the rider wrote 'Ok can, thanks' at 10:47:03, and her own filing records 'I said ok in the chat'. A fare complaint raised at 18:42:11, some eight hours after the trip ended at 11:04:11, is not an objection at the point of deviation, and it cannot retroactively un-agree a deviation the rider accepted in the chat while the vehicle was still on the road.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-06012"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-24"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.9
    },
    {
      "text": "The 4.80 SGD the rider claims has no basis in the policy's arithmetic. POL-RD-24 fixes the only sum the matrix can return on this record at the excess distance fare - deviation_km times fare_breakdown.per_km_rate_sgd, without surge - which is 1.40 x 0.72 = 1.01 SGD, and that only on rows (b) and (d), neither of which applies here. The ledger confirms per_km_rate_sgd 0.72, total_charged 21.41 and refund_issued_sgd 0.00, so the claimed figure is overstated several times over on the rider's own best case.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-06012", "EV-TRIP-06012"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-24"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.derived.money.excess_distance_fare_sgd",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The notice and the acknowledgement do not stand or fall on the impaired chat export. The COMPLETE trip record, weight 1.0, independently lists MSG-06012-003 (driver, 10:46:33) and MSG-06012-004 (rider, 10:47:03) in its messages_during_trip block, and POL-GEN-02(2) takes the highest weight among independent artifacts carrying the deciding fact. The single impairment in this record - the chat log at 0.9 for SCHEMA_VERSION_MISMATCH - therefore does not lower the weight of the agreed-deviation finding, and I name it rather than presenting it as clean.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-06012", "EV-CHAT-06012"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "This is a case the AI may finish on this record. The contested amount is 4.80 SGD, and the facts that decide it - the recorded distances, the message timestamps, the advisory window and its type - all rest on COMPLETE artifacts at weight 1.0, the only impairment being a 0.9 schema tag on the chat export. Whatever elevated confidence POL-GEN-22 requires where a profile carries fraud flags is met on this record, and POL-RD-25's condition on an AI ruling is satisfied, so no escalation is called for.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-06012", "EV-TRIP-06012", "EV-FARE-06012"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-22", "POL-RD-25"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties: this dispute goes to a human reviewer (ESCALATE). No money moves now — the disputed SGD 4.80 is held, not refunded to the rider and not collected from the driver, and no compensation is payable.\n\nWhat the record establishes. The platform's recorded distances (EV-TRIP-06012) give a deviation of 1.40 km — 17.6 km driven against a 16.2 km recommended route — above the 1.0 km tolerance in POL-RD-22, and the driver-device trace (EV-GPS-06012) shows which route was taken and when. At the ledger's SGD 0.72 per km (EV-FARE-06012) the excess-distance fare is SGD 1.01, not the SGD 4.80 claimed.\n\nTraffic justification (POL-RD-23). The LTA advisory (EV-ADVIS-06012-01) is a HEAVY_TRAFFIC — a congestion-class — advisory on the Central Expressway towards the City, valid 10:16 to 11:26, overlapping the trip (10:36 to 11:04) and covering the 10:49:23 deviation. The CTE is a leg of the recommended route (Canberra Link, SLE, CTE, Balestier Road), the advisory is in the direction of travel, and its position (after Ang Mo Kig Ave 1, towards the PIE) lies on the stretch the recommended route would have used south of where the driver left it. It therefore intersects the recommended route, and the reroute is traffic-justified. The rider is right that the driver's own chat assertion is not traffic data, but that is immaterial: the advisory, not the assertion, carries the justification.\n\nInforming and agreement (POL-RD-21). The in-app chat (EV-CHAT-06012) shows the driver told the rider at 10:46:33 and the rider replied 'Ok can, thanks' at 10:47:03, both before the deviation at 10:49:23. The deviation was therefore agreed, and row (a) of the POL-RD-24 matrix — traffic-justified, informed and agreed, over 1 km — would give no refund. The rider's contrary arguments that the advisory fails the intersection limb and that row (d) refunds SGD 1.01 are rejected for the reason above.\n\nWhy the AI cannot finish it. The chat export is impaired at weight 0.9 (issue SCHEMA_VERSION_MISMATCH), and the informing-and-agreement rests on it. The trip record's messages_during_trip block repeats the same message ids and times but not their text; it would not support the agreement with the chat removed, so it is not an independent carrier, and the confidence this ruling can carry is capped at 0.9 under POL-GEN-02(2). The driver's profile carries fraud_flags = 2, so POL-GEN-22 requires a confidence of 0.95 for an AI ruling, and POL-RD-25 escalates a route deviation where that is not met. No row of the POL-RD-24 matrix can be entered at 0.95: row (a) turns on the 0.9 chat, while rows (b) and (d) are contradicted by the record (the rider was informed; the reroute is traffic-justified).\n\nOpen question for the reviewer: whether the acknowledgment in the impaired chat export, on its own, supports the agreed-deviation finding at the confidence the fraud flag demands. Route deviation carries no referral clause in this version."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

