    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To Rider R-15817 and Driver D-43200: the AI cannot finalise this one, so it goes to a human reviewer, and no money moves while it is held.\n\nWhat is settled. The deviation is not in doubt. The platform's trip record EV-TRIP-06012 records 17.60 km driven against a 16.20 km recommended route, a deviation of 1.40 km (POL-RD-22). That is above the 1.0 km tolerance, so the case sits in the over-1-km part of the POL-RD-24 matrix, and the rider's 4.80 SGD headline is not the matrix's measure: the excess distance fare is 1.40 km x 0.72 SGD per km = 1.01 SGD, not 4.80 (EV-FARE-06012).\n\nThe reroute is traffic-justified. The LTA advisory EV-ADVIS-06012-01 is a HEAVY_TRAFFIC (congestion-class) advisory on the Central Expressway (CTE) towards the City, valid 10:16-11:26, overlapping the trip (10:36-11:04). Its derived fields leave the route-intersection for the Judge, and on its road (the CTE, a leg of the recommended route) and its direction (city-bound, the direction of travel) it lies on the recommended route, so POL-RD-23 is satisfied. I therefore reject the rider's claim that the intersection limb is not made out: the null derived fields are a hook for the Judge's own reading of road, direction and window, not a missing fact.\n\nOn the merits this points to row (a): the driver informed the rider before deviating and the rider agreed. The chat EV-CHAT-06012 shows the driver's message at 10:46:33 ('Hi, CTE jam until PIE, I go Upper Thomson then Thomson Road ok?') and the rider's reply at 10:47:03 ('Ok can, thanks'), both before the deviation was detected at 10:49:23 (POL-RD-21). Row (a) would leave the rider carrying the charge.\n\nWhy the AI cannot enter that row. The only artifact that carries the content of those two messages is the chat log, and the pre-pass marks EV-CHAT-06012 IMPAIRED at weight 0.9 on issue SCHEMA_VERSION_MISMATCH. The driver's argument that the COMPLETE trip record independently carries the notice and the acknowledgment is rejected: EV-TRIP-06012's messages_during_trip block lists only message ids, senders and timestamps, not the words exchanged, so it does not carry the agreed-deviation fact and cannot lift the cap. Under POL-GEN-02(2) my confidence is capped at 0.9. Because the driver's profile carries fraud_flags of 2 (EV-DPROF-06012), POL-GEN-22 requires 0.95 for an AI ruling here, whatever the 4.80 SGD value. 0.9 falls below 0.95, so POL-RD-25 and POL-GEN-22 require the case to go to a human reviewer. The rider's fallback that the case should instead be resolved on row (d) is also rejected: where the row that fits cannot be entered at the required confidence, the policy does not license substituting a different row.\n\nFor the human reviewer, the open question is whether the rider's acknowledgment in the chat is accepted at full weight and the traffic justification confirmed; that decides between row (a) (NO_ACTION, no refund) and any refund row, and the excess distance fare on the matrix is 1.01 SGD, not the 4.80 SGD claimed. The disputed sum is held, not collected or refunded. No clause of the route-deviation policy produces a referral here."
